{
  "notes": [
    "Single shared entity alias map (see CLAUDE.md 'Entity normalization / alias map').",
    "Consumed by BOTH the TS path (apps/web/lib/server/entity-aliases.ts, used by neon.ts's prepareMentionBatch) and the Python path (entity_aliases.py, used by _normalize_enrichment_payload in run_financial_news_pipeline.py and app.py) - edit this file, never fork per-language copies.",
    "Matching happens in normalized space (lowercased, punctuation collapsed to spaces - see normalizeMentionValue / normalize_mention_value), so aliases here can be written in natural casing/punctuation.",
    "'the Commission' maps to SEC per the CLAUDE.md spec; in rare CFTC-context documents this will mis-attribute, an accepted tradeoff since this corpus is overwhelmingly SEC-centric.",
    "Keep canonical labels short and display-ready - they replace the stored mention value when an alias is collapsed."
  ],
